                <h4>2. Operational Manifestations &amp; Procedural Protocols</h4>

                <div class="statute-box">
                    <h3>c) Electronic FIR (e-FIR) Registration</h3>
                    <p class="editable-field" contenteditable="true">
                        Complainants are now legally empowered to report cognizable offenses digitally, entirely removing the baseline requirement to physically visit a physical police station to initiate the initial informational entry.
                    </p>
                    <div class="forensic-observation">
                        <strong>Forensic Observation: Validation Mechanism</strong>
                        <span class="editable-field" contenteditable="true">While an e-FIR can be lodged via electronic communication, the BNSS requires the informant to sign the document within three days for it to be officially recorded as the foundational starting point of the investigation.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="statute-box">
                    <h3>d) Court Orders &amp; Digital Signatures</h3>
                    <p class="editable-field" contenteditable="true">
                        Investigators must still secure formalized search warrants or express court permissions to force access to private physical premises or sensitive corporate institutional storage architectures.
                    </p>
                    <div class="forensic-observation">
                        <strong>Forensic Observation: Workflow Acceleration</strong>
                        <span class="editable-field" contenteditable="true">The new era permits the production, transmission, and signing of summonses, warrants, and judicial orders in an electronic format. This significantly speeds up the legal pipeline when dealing with time-sensitive volatile data or rapid cloud forensic responses.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="statute-box">
                    <h3>e) Chain of Custody &amp; Digital Preservation</h3>
                    <p class="editable-field" contenteditable="true">
                        <strong>Authenticity and Integrity:</strong> The strict tracking ledger must document every transition of physical or digital evidence from the precise point of seizure down to its presentation before a magistrate.
                    </p>
                    <div class="forensic-observation">
                        <strong>Forensic Observation: Mathematical Validation</strong>
                        <span class="editable-field" contenteditable="true">With the shift toward digital evidence, the chain of custody must incorporate cryptographic verification formulas (SHA-256/MD5 hashes) alongside physical signatures. This mathematical locking ensures complete data integrity, proving that no data blocks were modified during transport or analysis.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

